1
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,005
(Supported by MCST and KOCCA)

2
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,006
(This drama is purely a work of fiction.)

3
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:09,487
(All scenes with child actors and animals were filmed safely.)

4
00:00:12,346 --> 00:00:18,060
(The day of the incident)

5
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:23,649
It's burning well.

6
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:32,074
What do we do with the phone and wallet?

7
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,868
We'd better burn them, right?

8
00:00:35,327 --> 00:00:36,787
You're crazy.

9
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:38,747
The phone will explode.

10
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:41,291
And don't ever turn the power on.

11
00:00:46,797 --> 00:00:48,215
Then what do we do with this?

12
00:00:48,966 --> 00:00:50,592
Dump it somewhere else?

13
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:53,470
But what if we dump it...

14
00:00:53,554 --> 00:00:55,264
and someone happens to pick it up?

15
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:57,516
No, wait.

16
00:00:59,476 --> 00:01:01,812
If the phone turns on elsewhere,

17
00:01:03,105 --> 00:01:04,940
that's where they'll trace him.

18
00:01:08,819 --> 00:01:09,903
Hold on.

19
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:13,782
It should be the same...

20
00:01:16,535 --> 00:01:17,744
for this credit card.

21
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:22,749
If it turns up in the middle of nowhere...

22
00:01:26,086 --> 00:01:28,088
Then no one will ever track us down.

23
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:33,260
Honey.

24
00:01:34,303 --> 00:01:35,721
We're geniuses.

25
00:01:37,431 --> 00:01:39,016
But where do we ditch these?

26
00:01:42,394 --> 00:01:43,979
Somewhere completely public.

27
00:02:31,943 --> 00:02:33,987
Right where you'd see it while taking a dump.

28
00:02:34,071 --> 00:02:35,197
Somewhere like that.

29
00:02:36,031 --> 00:02:37,115
You get me?

30
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:10,273
I'm done. How about the phone?

31
00:03:10,357 --> 00:03:11,608
Not here.

32
00:03:11,692 --> 00:03:13,610
The park is crawling with CCTV cameras.

33
00:03:14,653 --> 00:03:17,239
There must be a safer way to handle this.

34
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:34,589
(Seasoned salt)

35
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:57,904
(The Affair Was Just The Beginning)

36
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:05,954
(Episode 6: Your Mom, My Dad)

37
00:04:05,996 --> 00:04:08,540
Where are you going at this hour?

38
00:04:08,623 --> 00:04:11,209
I swear, I'll never contact her again.

39
00:04:11,293 --> 00:04:12,585
Look, honey.

40
00:04:12,586 --> 00:04:13,920
Look at this.

41
00:04:14,004 --> 00:04:15,254
This is Min Seo's mom.

42
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:17,632
I'm blocking her right in front of you.

43
00:04:17,716 --> 00:04:18,759
Honey.

44
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:21,761
She's blocked. Honey, look.

45
00:04:21,762 --> 00:04:24,973
Honey, I'm completely done with her. I promise.

46
00:04:25,015 --> 00:04:27,684
(Two days after the incident)

47
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:30,645
Why did I do that?

48
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:31,938
Goodness.

49
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:43,825
Dad.

50
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:45,619
Did you and Mom fight?

51
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:49,080
Is it because of me?

52
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:51,916
Is that why she left?

53
00:04:51,917 --> 00:04:53,418
No, Ye Ji.

54
00:04:53,919 --> 00:04:55,212
It's nothing like that.

55
00:04:57,172 --> 00:04:58,173
Ye Ji.

56
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:00,383
This has nothing to do with you.

57
00:05:01,176 --> 00:05:02,177
Okay?

58
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:58,057
Go tell your dad everything. Tell him you're innocent.

59
00:05:58,567 --> 00:06:00,167
That I was the one who hit him, not you.

60
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:01,485
Just tell him!

61
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:03,154
I'll just go to prison.

62
00:06:03,238 --> 00:06:04,990
Isn't that what you want?

63
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:13,725
Hi, Ye Ji.

64
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:15,977
Hi, Min Seo.

65
00:07:17,479 --> 00:07:18,980
Ye Ji, I...

66
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:25,528
Are you crying?

67
00:07:26,738 --> 00:07:28,198
My mom...

68
00:07:29,324 --> 00:07:30,951
left home.

69
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:34,329
What do I do, Min Seo?

70
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:44,381
(Thanks for the ride today. It must've been awkward.)

71
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:48,218
(I'm sorry, but can you check if the video's deleted?)

72
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:23,919
The comments are blowing up.

73
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,504
So many of our crew are...

74
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:27,549
showing interest in Apfel Kitchen.

75
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:31,135
That's right. This is the exact same kitchen setup as in my home.

76
00:08:31,136 --> 00:08:33,721
Let's take a closer look today.

77
00:08:33,722 --> 00:08:35,849
The colour alone is incredibly luxurious.

78
00:08:35,932 --> 00:08:37,808
And the touch feature here...

79
00:08:37,809 --> 00:08:39,309
makes it very convenient.

80
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:42,147
Plus, this can be customized to fit any space, right?

81
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:44,648
Yes, everything is fully customizable.

82
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:47,068
So you can tailor the height, width, and colour...

83
00:08:47,152 --> 00:08:49,904
to match your space.

84
00:08:50,238 --> 00:08:52,490
I personally love this part right here.

85
00:08:52,532 --> 00:08:55,325
This Zen-style design.

86
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:57,287
You know how Zen style is.

87
00:08:57,370 --> 00:09:00,540
It brings such elegance and luxury,

88
00:09:00,623 --> 00:09:03,208
almost like displaying a fine work of art in your own home.

89
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:05,711
And since our showroom is right by Gangnam Station,

90
00:09:05,712 --> 00:09:07,796
dropping by for a consultation couldn't be easier.

91
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:10,216
Wow, that makes it so easy to get to.

92
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:13,510
Cut. That was perfect.

93
00:09:13,511 --> 00:09:14,678
Now, the next shot.

94
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:16,264
Please get this one more time.

95
00:09:16,306 --> 00:09:18,682
- Here? - Yes, and back here.

96
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:20,894
- Up to here. - Min Su, come.

97
00:09:23,438 --> 00:09:24,689
Gosh, I'm tired.

98
00:09:26,775 --> 00:09:29,444
(My Hong: Please.)

99
00:09:35,075 --> 00:09:36,076
Min Su.

100
00:09:36,326 --> 00:09:38,286
Capture these three details right here.

101
00:09:38,369 --> 00:09:41,081
One moment. The homeroom teacher keeps calling.

102
00:10:20,912 --> 00:10:22,664
You're taking Min Seo right now?

103
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:24,748
- Hello. - Who gives you the right?

104
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:26,542
What are you scheming this time?

105
00:10:26,543 --> 00:10:28,628
With the abuse and the disappearance,

106
00:10:28,711 --> 00:10:30,797
you're clearly unfit to be a parent.

107
00:10:31,089 --> 00:10:33,508
You faked all those reports!

108
00:10:34,843 --> 00:10:36,553
You think I'm just going to take it?

109
00:10:38,388 --> 00:10:40,098
Why? Are you going to sue me?

110
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:43,518
Great. Attorney Choi has been dying to meet you anyway.

111
00:10:45,562 --> 00:10:46,854
Attorney Choi?

112
00:10:46,855 --> 00:10:48,648
Hello. Long time no see.

113
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:51,234
She is a child abuser, so please arrest her right away.

114
00:10:57,157 --> 00:10:58,283
Whatever.

115
00:10:59,993 --> 00:11:02,787
Talk to Attorney Choi from now on.

116
00:11:03,705 --> 00:11:04,873
Hello.

117
00:11:04,956 --> 00:11:06,499
Hello. Thank you for the hard work.

118
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:09,919
Hello, ma'am.

119
00:11:09,961 --> 00:11:10,961
- Hello. - Hello.

120
00:11:10,962 --> 00:11:12,255
- Hello. - Hello, Dr. Joo.

121
00:11:25,018 --> 00:11:26,144
Ye Ji.

122
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:29,147
I didn't get a chance to ask yesterday, but that video...

123
00:11:30,148 --> 00:11:31,316
Hi, Dad.

124
00:11:32,901 --> 00:11:33,902
What?

125
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:41,241
Taxi.

126
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:45,163
(Available)

127
00:12:08,978 --> 00:12:11,105
The number cannot be reached. You'll be...

128
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:17,903
(Why won't you pick up? Is it done or not?)

129
00:12:17,904 --> 00:12:19,447
(Call me as soon as you get this.)

130
00:12:26,496 --> 00:12:28,831
(Min Seo's academy)

131
00:12:30,041 --> 00:12:31,167
Hello?

132
00:12:34,087 --> 00:12:35,129
She didn't?

133
00:12:45,306 --> 00:12:47,599
- Oh, my. - You... You're up.

134
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,477
- I didn't mean to wake you. - I'm sorry.

135
00:12:50,561 --> 00:12:51,979
- Careful. - Thank you.

136
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:53,356
The IV's almost done.

137
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:55,275
I must've startled you.

138
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:57,735
I rarely pass out like this.

139
00:12:58,194 --> 00:13:01,030
Oh, anyone can pass out.

140
00:13:01,739 --> 00:13:04,367
Let's see. Looks like it's done.

141
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:06,202
- Let me remove this for you. - Okay.

142
00:13:12,292 --> 00:13:15,670
If you don't look after yourself early on,

143
00:13:15,753 --> 00:13:17,880
you'll end up regretting it when it's too late.

144
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:21,009
Tell me about it.

145
00:13:22,218 --> 00:13:24,804
But what if I'm regretting everything I've lost?

146
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:28,683
Here.

147
00:13:28,766 --> 00:13:30,393
- Oh, okay. - Hold some pressure here.

148
00:13:32,854 --> 00:13:34,147
Truth be told,

149
00:13:35,273 --> 00:13:37,150
this isn't an expansion.

150
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,446
I lost it all to my ex-wife.

151
00:13:43,239 --> 00:13:44,657
I gave up...

152
00:13:44,741 --> 00:13:47,035
my child and the house to her.

153
00:13:47,452 --> 00:13:49,829
It felt like nothing was working out for me.

154
00:13:49,912 --> 00:13:52,081
But now that I'm opening a new clinic,

155
00:13:52,749 --> 00:13:54,417
and moreover,

156
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:57,879
with you doing the renovations, I feel more encouraged.

157
00:13:57,962 --> 00:13:59,380
- Hello. - Hello.

158
00:13:59,464 --> 00:14:01,049
I heard my wife passed out.

159
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:06,387
From my child to my husband, nothing is going my way.

160
00:14:06,471 --> 00:14:08,222
- It's this way. - Oh, here?

161
00:14:08,306 --> 00:14:09,891
Life's not all that special.

162
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:12,268
- You just have to get through it... - Mom.

163
00:14:14,145 --> 00:14:15,438
- Honey. - Hello.

164
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:16,606
Hey, Ye Ji.

165
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:20,693
Ms. Yoon called and said you suddenly passed out.

166
00:14:21,277 --> 00:14:22,362
Honey.

167
00:14:22,904 --> 00:14:24,072
Are you okay?

168
00:14:24,906 --> 00:14:26,406
Dr. Joo, could I talk to you for a bit?

169
00:14:26,407 --> 00:14:28,034
You must've been so stressed.

170
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:29,744
Let's hurry home.

171
00:14:31,371 --> 00:14:34,415
About the lighting you wanted, we'll put two magnetic lights here.

172
00:14:34,499 --> 00:14:36,584
And this side will feature cove lighting.

173
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:38,169
- Oh, this side? - Yes.

174
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:40,003
If there are any other lights you want...

175
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:41,380
Let's go home.

176
00:14:41,381 --> 00:14:42,757
- This side... - Okay.

177
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,425
Let's go home. Rest at home, honey.

178
00:15:36,185 --> 00:15:37,311
Min Seo.

179
00:15:39,105 --> 00:15:40,273
Mom?

180
00:15:40,356 --> 00:15:42,191
Why did you come back here?

181
00:15:42,275 --> 00:15:43,860
I'm so scared, Mom.

182
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:45,445
What do I do?

183
00:15:46,279 --> 00:15:48,156
It's okay, Min Seo.

184
00:15:48,239 --> 00:15:49,740
It's going to be okay.

185
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:51,409
I will...

186
00:15:51,492 --> 00:15:53,327
I will make sure of it.

187
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:16,559
(Kids Guard: GPS Location Tracker App)

188
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:20,313
(Downloading)

189
00:16:20,396 --> 00:16:21,564
(Installed)

190
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:06,734
Well...

191
00:17:26,254 --> 00:17:30,967
(Five days after the incident)

192
00:17:51,946 --> 00:17:53,072
Wait.

193
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:54,824
These are...

194
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:57,410
You're giving these to me?

195
00:17:57,493 --> 00:17:59,495
I got them as a gift a while back,

196
00:17:59,579 --> 00:18:02,456
but I don't see myself ever wearing them.

197
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:06,168
People can mistake someone else's shoes for their own.

198
00:18:06,627 --> 00:18:08,796
Are you sure you want to give these away?

199
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:13,301
Regardless of my intent, I could be charged...

200
00:18:13,384 --> 00:18:16,429
with embezzlement of lost property if I refuse to return them.

201
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:19,890
Embezzlement? Give me a break.

202
00:18:20,308 --> 00:18:21,475
Goodness.

203
00:18:22,143 --> 00:18:24,103
Are you perhaps a lawyer?

204
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:27,732
Yes, I run a small practice.

205
00:18:28,149 --> 00:18:30,860
Oh, I see.

206
00:18:34,405 --> 00:18:36,782
These are really hard to get ahold of.

207
00:18:38,034 --> 00:18:39,201
Are they expensive?

208
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:43,331
You have no idea, do you?

209
00:18:43,414 --> 00:18:44,999
These are absolutely...

210
00:18:50,588 --> 00:18:53,090
Sol was here recently, wasn't he?

211
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:55,509
Yes, he left with a guest.

212
00:18:56,886 --> 00:18:57,887
Is that the guy?

213
00:18:58,763 --> 00:19:00,556
Yes, that's him.

214
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:05,686
Did he say anything in particular?

215
00:19:08,439 --> 00:19:09,732
"Anything in particular"?

216
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:13,861
Oh, he said he was a lawyer or something.

217
00:19:13,944 --> 00:19:15,154
A lawyer?

218
00:19:15,237 --> 00:19:18,616
Yes, Mr. Sol told us to treat him with special care.

219
00:19:24,205 --> 00:19:26,874
He doesn't look like a lawyer.

220
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:51,732
Look.

221
00:19:52,024 --> 00:19:55,319
The name's Choi Sang Cheol. He's a lawyer.

222
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:58,989
This guy defended the Hanram-dong drug party case...

223
00:19:59,073 --> 00:20:03,243
and the major prostitution case that happened recently.

224
00:20:03,244 --> 00:20:04,704
This guy will do anything for money,

225
00:20:04,787 --> 00:20:09,457
blackmail, forgery, you name it.

226
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:12,920
It's not my place to say, but the guy is a total lowlife.

227
00:20:14,130 --> 00:20:17,425
He doesn't seem big enough to pull a job on Sol.

228
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:20,136
Does he have any guys backing him?

229
00:20:20,970 --> 00:20:21,971
Now, look.

230
00:20:23,139 --> 00:20:24,849
Here's my careful guess.

231
00:20:25,975 --> 00:20:27,017
What is this?

232
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:30,354
Ko Du Sik, the suspect in the Maguk-dong dismemberment murder.

233
00:20:30,438 --> 00:20:31,564
Remember him?

234
00:20:32,398 --> 00:20:33,941
This case was...

235
00:20:34,024 --> 00:20:36,902
closed for lack of evidence.

236
00:20:36,986 --> 00:20:38,779
But then,

237
00:20:38,863 --> 00:20:41,449
it was all Choi Sang Cheol's doing.

238
00:20:42,324 --> 00:20:43,951
That's the weird part.

239
00:20:44,034 --> 00:20:46,912
It was a clear-cut case. Anyone could see that.

240
00:20:46,996 --> 00:20:49,874
But he got off, which supposedly means...

241
00:20:50,499 --> 00:20:52,752
Ko Du Sik now owes Choi Sang Cheol...

242
00:20:53,461 --> 00:20:55,379
absolute loyalty.

243
00:20:56,046 --> 00:20:58,716
If there's anyone behind him,

244
00:20:58,799 --> 00:21:01,635
it's likely Ko Du Sik.

245
00:21:02,762 --> 00:21:03,971
- Okay? - So,

246
00:21:04,054 --> 00:21:07,516
is it possible to locate these two?

247
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:11,353
It's possible for Ko Du Sik,

248
00:21:11,937 --> 00:21:14,732
but Choi Sang Cheol...

249
00:21:17,318 --> 00:21:18,527
You see,

250
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:20,946
security is...

251
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:23,991
pretty tight these days.

252
00:21:24,658 --> 00:21:27,702
And messing with a lawyer...

253
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:31,248
could backfire on us.

254
00:21:32,166 --> 00:21:33,584
Then, let's start...

255
00:21:34,335 --> 00:21:36,712
by meeting Ko Du Sik...

256
00:21:37,254 --> 00:21:38,589
for a peaceful talk.

257
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:40,716
What? You want to meet him in person?

258
00:21:44,178 --> 00:21:47,056
What were you doing on March 30?

259
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:49,307
March 30?

260
00:21:49,308 --> 00:21:50,392
What was I up to?

261
00:21:55,898 --> 00:21:57,900
Darn, I don't remember.

262
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:02,279
Have a drink of this.

263
00:22:02,488 --> 00:22:03,906
It helps clear your mind.

264
00:22:08,661 --> 00:22:10,329
My mind is perfectly clear right now.

265
00:22:10,788 --> 00:22:12,623
It doesn't look like it.

266
00:22:17,378 --> 00:22:18,379
Well...

267
00:22:20,673 --> 00:22:23,008
Can I take a quick look at your phone?

268
00:22:31,976 --> 00:22:33,216
What do you want with my phone?

269
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:36,188
It'll only take a moment.

270
00:22:38,107 --> 00:22:39,567
Wow, it smells great.

271
00:22:40,025 --> 00:22:42,152
Finish it.

272
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:45,030
I brewed this tea myself.

273
00:22:45,114 --> 00:22:46,447
Once you drink it,

274
00:22:46,448 --> 00:22:49,118
you won't pass out, no matter how severely you're beaten.

275
00:22:55,374 --> 00:22:57,209
You want my phone.

276
00:22:58,752 --> 00:23:00,379
My phone...

277
00:23:01,255 --> 00:23:02,464
Here it is.

278
00:23:09,263 --> 00:23:10,389
Mr. Do.

279
00:23:10,890 --> 00:23:14,517
I dug through everything around March 30,

280
00:23:14,518 --> 00:23:16,103
but there's nothing.

281
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:19,856
Maybe Choi Sang Cheol acted alone.

282
00:23:19,857 --> 00:23:21,692
Isn't it obvious?

283
00:23:21,817 --> 00:23:25,279
Sol wouldn't get taken down by a guy like Choi Sang Cheol.

284
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:28,574
He's definitely got backing.

285
00:23:28,991 --> 00:23:30,993
We need to find them and crush them all at once.

286
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:34,121
Look at the camera in 1, 2, 3.

287
00:23:35,414 --> 00:23:37,374
In 1, 2, 3.

288
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:40,586
- Thank you. - My pleasure.

289
00:23:40,669 --> 00:23:41,670
Thank you.

290
00:23:45,966 --> 00:23:48,427
What a superstar.

291
00:23:48,510 --> 00:23:51,512
- Everyone recognises you, man. - Oh, please.

292
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:53,223
I was coming out of the bathroom and...

293
00:23:54,141 --> 00:23:55,893
- Let's clink. - Sure.

294
00:23:55,976 --> 00:23:57,478
- Cheers. - Cheers.

295
00:24:12,242 --> 00:24:13,619
You poured too much soju in it.

296
00:24:15,204 --> 00:24:17,538
You can't be this bad at making a soju bomb.

297
00:24:17,539 --> 00:24:18,623
Seriously.

298
00:24:18,624 --> 00:24:19,791
Hand it over. I'll do it.

299
00:24:19,792 --> 00:24:20,834
Pour me a glass.

300
00:24:27,883 --> 00:24:28,926
This...

301
00:24:32,846 --> 00:24:34,056
Hold on.

302
00:24:37,643 --> 00:24:39,311
Oh, gosh.

303
00:24:39,395 --> 00:24:40,937
Hey, be careful.

304
00:24:40,938 --> 00:24:42,022
There.

305
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:44,817
All right, up we go.

306
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:46,610
Watch your step.

307
00:24:47,903 --> 00:24:48,904
Gosh.

308
00:24:48,988 --> 00:24:51,323
How did you get this drunk?

309
00:24:51,407 --> 00:24:53,117
Come on.

310
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:55,119
Watch the stairs.

311
00:24:55,202 --> 00:24:57,329
Okay, punch in the code.

312
00:24:57,413 --> 00:24:58,497
What's the code?

313
00:24:58,580 --> 00:25:00,833
- The code... - Okay, careful.

314
00:25:02,501 --> 00:25:04,294
Okay, there we go.

315
00:25:04,378 --> 00:25:05,504
Let's go inside.

316
00:25:05,587 --> 00:25:07,256
Come on, man.

317
00:25:07,339 --> 00:25:09,049
You drank way too much today.

318
00:25:57,389 --> 00:25:58,515
Who are you?

319
00:26:05,314 --> 00:26:07,316
You must be Ye Ji.

320
00:26:08,150 --> 00:26:10,694
You're as pretty as I've heard.

321
00:26:13,614 --> 00:26:16,949
I'm a close friend of Jae Hong's.

322
00:26:16,950 --> 00:26:19,620
He got so drunk that I brought him home.

323
00:26:20,329 --> 00:26:22,455
He said... What was that?

324
00:26:22,456 --> 00:26:24,832
Oh, he said the hangover medicine was around here.

325
00:26:24,833 --> 00:26:26,292
But I can't find it anywhere.

326
00:26:26,293 --> 00:26:27,294
Do you know where it is?

327
00:26:28,128 --> 00:26:29,588
Not in there.

328
00:26:31,340 --> 00:26:33,008
Oh, not here.

329
00:26:35,260 --> 00:26:36,303
No wonder...

330
00:26:36,720 --> 00:26:38,764
I couldn't find it.

331
00:26:40,682 --> 00:26:43,727
Maybe you can get it for him.

332
00:26:43,852 --> 00:26:45,604
I need to get going.

333
00:26:45,938 --> 00:26:47,231
Okay.

334
00:26:48,524 --> 00:26:50,359
I'd better come again another time.

335
00:26:51,193 --> 00:26:52,319
Gosh, you're pretty.

336
00:27:11,255 --> 00:27:14,550
(Your husband's lawyer has a lot of shady business going on.)

337
00:27:26,562 --> 00:27:30,315
The number cannot be reached. You'll be directed...

338
00:27:42,202 --> 00:27:43,787
Wait, honey.

339
00:27:43,829 --> 00:27:45,164
You look stunning today.

340
00:27:45,998 --> 00:27:49,084
Didn't you wear that on our anniversary last year?

341
00:27:49,126 --> 00:27:50,502
The one I picked out.

342
00:27:51,545 --> 00:27:52,921
I have a great memory, don't I?

343
00:27:55,382 --> 00:27:57,217
Wait, are you...

344
00:27:57,384 --> 00:27:58,843
going somewhere today?

345
00:27:58,844 --> 00:28:00,804
Why wear that outfit all of a sudden?

346
00:28:01,305 --> 00:28:04,391
Honey, are you going to be late today?

347
00:28:05,017 --> 00:28:06,310
Where are you going?

348
00:28:06,393 --> 00:28:07,810
Who are you meeting up with?

349
00:28:07,811 --> 00:28:09,354
Are you going to be late?

350
00:28:09,396 --> 00:28:11,523
Honey, where are you...

351
00:28:11,565 --> 00:28:13,567
Who are you meeting?

352
00:28:13,609 --> 00:28:15,861
Is it a lunch appointment? Or work?

353
00:28:15,944 --> 00:28:16,945
- Hello. - No.

354
00:28:17,029 --> 00:28:18,155
Hi, Min Seo.

355
00:28:18,780 --> 00:28:20,616
What do you mean, no?

356
00:28:20,908 --> 00:28:24,661
No to work or to a lunch appointment?

357
00:28:26,163 --> 00:28:28,582
Honey, why don't we grab dinner together later?

358
00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:31,210
Where do you finish up? I'll come to you.

359
00:28:31,293 --> 00:28:32,502
No, thanks.

360
00:28:35,839 --> 00:28:36,965
Honey.

361
00:28:37,049 --> 00:28:38,883
Drive safely, okay?

362
00:28:38,884 --> 00:28:39,927
See you.

363
00:28:51,396 --> 00:28:54,274
Jae Hong, why don't you ever pick up my calls?

364
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:57,653
We can't do this anymore, Ms. Ahn.

365
00:28:57,736 --> 00:28:58,820
That's not it.

366
00:29:01,073 --> 00:29:03,158
Soo Jung, you're making it too hard for me.

367
00:29:03,242 --> 00:29:05,911
Let's just keep the good memories as they are.

368
00:29:05,994 --> 00:29:07,996
Please, Soo Jung.

369
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:09,790
No, it's about Choi Sang Cheol.

370
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,302
Why are you girls so quiet?

371
00:29:24,680 --> 00:29:25,722
What's going on?

372
00:29:26,348 --> 00:29:28,225
You two didn't fight, did you?

373
00:29:29,059 --> 00:29:30,560
Absolutely not.

374
00:29:31,061 --> 00:29:32,604
We're rock solid.

375
00:29:33,397 --> 00:29:34,731
Right, Min Seo?

376
00:29:36,108 --> 00:29:37,109
What?

377
00:29:37,567 --> 00:29:38,777
Oh, yes.

378
00:29:44,825 --> 00:29:46,576
- Mrs. Park. - What is it?

379
00:29:47,244 --> 00:29:49,079
Did you...

380
00:29:51,039 --> 00:29:53,917
delete the video?

381
00:29:56,837 --> 00:29:58,088
Well...

382
00:29:58,880 --> 00:30:00,090
Let me...

383
00:30:02,050 --> 00:30:03,844
take care of that on my end.

384
00:30:05,012 --> 00:30:07,848
I'm sure you handled it well,

385
00:30:07,931 --> 00:30:09,433
but if you only deleted the file,

386
00:30:09,516 --> 00:30:12,811
formatting the entire USB is supposedly much safer.

387
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:14,812
If it's too much hassle, I...

388
00:30:14,813 --> 00:30:16,023
Min Seo.

389
00:30:16,773 --> 00:30:18,317
Don't concern yourself with it.

390
00:30:24,489 --> 00:30:27,451
Right. Don't worry, Min Seo.

391
00:30:33,832 --> 00:30:35,500
- Are you serious? - Yes.

392
00:30:35,584 --> 00:30:36,585
So Choi Sang Cheol is...

393
00:30:37,377 --> 00:30:40,547
- your ex-husband's lawyer? - Yes.

394
00:30:40,630 --> 00:30:42,799
How is this even possible by chance?

395
00:30:43,342 --> 00:30:46,762
What if it wasn't a coincidence? What if he approached on purpose?

396
00:30:47,346 --> 00:30:48,347
What?

397
00:30:49,181 --> 00:30:50,265
Where is this coming from?

398
00:30:51,391 --> 00:30:52,934
I think Choi Sang Cheol...

399
00:30:53,018 --> 00:30:55,020
approached you specifically to use...

400
00:30:55,729 --> 00:30:58,273
our relationship in court, so think carefully.

401
00:30:58,899 --> 00:31:01,026
Are you sure he didn't say anything else?

402
00:31:01,109 --> 00:31:02,319
Jae Hong.

403
00:31:02,402 --> 00:31:04,404
Please tell me you didn't say anything weird.

404
00:31:06,948 --> 00:31:10,494
I was so drunk that I don't remember much.

405
00:31:11,495 --> 00:31:15,165
This explains why he gave me those sneakers out of nowhere.

406
00:31:15,248 --> 00:31:16,500
They're rare ones too.

407
00:31:16,958 --> 00:31:18,001
Sneakers?

408
00:31:19,002 --> 00:31:21,129
I don't think I said much,

409
00:31:21,963 --> 00:31:25,216
but I was so drunk.

410
00:31:25,217 --> 00:31:26,676
Strangely,

411
00:31:26,885 --> 00:31:28,178
my memory is fuzzy.

412
00:31:28,637 --> 00:31:31,473
- You don't remember? - No.

413
00:31:31,556 --> 00:31:33,517
Jae Hong, you're already outside.

414
00:31:33,642 --> 00:31:36,311
- Why are you so early? - We're late.

415
00:31:36,561 --> 00:31:38,063
Oh, are we? Let's go.

416
00:31:38,855 --> 00:31:40,857
- Let's talk later via Gogo Used Goods. - I...

417
00:31:42,275 --> 00:31:43,735
Darn.

418
00:31:43,819 --> 00:31:47,072
I knew it. There's no way he gave me those for free.

419
00:31:53,120 --> 00:31:54,954
Did he spike my drink?

420
00:31:54,955 --> 00:31:55,955
What was that? Spike?

421
00:31:55,956 --> 00:31:56,957
What?

422
00:31:58,417 --> 00:31:59,751
No, it's nothing.

423
00:32:00,752 --> 00:32:01,752
(My friend Attorney Choi Sang Cheol)

424
00:32:01,753 --> 00:32:02,921
This punk...

425
00:32:05,048 --> 00:32:06,799
Hello? Hi, Jae Hong.

426
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:08,050
Are you feeling okay?

427
00:32:08,051 --> 00:32:09,469
We should have another drink.

428
00:32:09,636 --> 00:32:12,180
How about your place this time?

429
00:32:12,264 --> 00:32:14,140
I've got some amazing liquor.

430
00:32:14,141 --> 00:32:15,391
I'll bring it over.

431
00:32:15,392 --> 00:32:16,435
Hey.

432
00:32:17,602 --> 00:32:20,063
Are you sure you actually go to that gym?

433
00:32:20,230 --> 00:32:21,231
Sorry?

434
00:32:21,481 --> 00:32:23,233
How come I never saw you?

435
00:32:23,316 --> 00:32:25,067
Maybe because I mostly go in the morning.

436
00:32:25,068 --> 00:32:26,236
And...

437
00:32:26,403 --> 00:32:27,737
those sneakers.

438
00:32:28,738 --> 00:32:31,824
Are you sure you got them as a gift and gave them to me...

439
00:32:31,825 --> 00:32:33,535
simply because you didn't wear them?

440
00:32:33,827 --> 00:32:35,787
What are you talking about?

441
00:32:35,954 --> 00:32:37,998
Hold on. There's something I need to tell you.

442
00:32:38,081 --> 00:32:39,166
Never mind.

443
00:32:40,208 --> 00:32:41,459
Hang up, you jerk.

444
00:32:41,460 --> 00:32:42,961
No, wait. Don't hang up.

445
00:32:48,633 --> 00:32:49,717
(My friend Attorney Choi Sang Cheol)

446
00:32:49,718 --> 00:32:51,511
This piece of...

447
00:32:54,598 --> 00:32:55,807
What?

448
00:32:57,184 --> 00:32:59,744
(I think there's a misunderstanding. I'll drop by your place...)

449
00:32:59,978 --> 00:33:01,605
Misunderstanding, my foot.

450
00:33:03,064 --> 00:33:06,818
(No, don't come.)

451
00:33:23,793 --> 00:33:25,085
Kyung Hee.

452
00:33:25,086 --> 00:33:26,671
- Hello, Dr. Joo. - Goodness.

453
00:33:27,130 --> 00:33:28,255
Oh, my.

454
00:33:28,256 --> 00:33:30,883
You look beautiful as always today.

455
00:33:30,884 --> 00:33:32,384
Oh, stop it.

456
00:33:32,385 --> 00:33:36,014
Hold on. Everyone might stare at you.

457
00:33:36,348 --> 00:33:39,600
Are you really okay with being recognised?

458
00:33:39,601 --> 00:33:41,685
Who cares?

459
00:33:41,686 --> 00:33:43,562
We're here for business.

460
00:33:43,563 --> 00:33:44,647
That's right, business.

461
00:33:44,648 --> 00:33:46,982
Shall we head up to the lounge and talk?

462
00:33:46,983 --> 00:33:48,693
- Sure. - Let's go.

463
00:33:55,367 --> 00:33:56,368
What's wrong?

464
00:34:04,417 --> 00:34:05,544
Wait, isn't that...

465
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:07,546
He's Chairwoman Jeong's secretary.

466
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:11,423
The Chairwoman must be here.

467
00:34:11,424 --> 00:34:13,009
She's a regular here, you see.

468
00:34:22,602 --> 00:34:23,978
Is something wrong?

469
00:34:23,979 --> 00:34:26,189
(Director Kwak: I'm currently driving.)

470
00:34:35,407 --> 00:34:37,200
(Why won't you pick up? Is it done or not?)

471
00:34:50,422 --> 00:34:51,548
It can't be.

472
00:35:24,205 --> 00:35:28,208
(The man who got hit by the car...)

473
00:35:28,209 --> 00:35:32,213
(Do you remember what he looked like?)

474
00:35:35,967 --> 00:35:39,137
(I don't want to talk about it. I'm too scared.)

475
00:36:08,083 --> 00:36:14,089
(Tools)

476
00:36:29,771 --> 00:36:31,211
- What are you doing? - Oh, my gosh.

477
00:36:33,942 --> 00:36:35,360
Mr. Na Sol.

478
00:36:35,443 --> 00:36:36,903
Are you serious right now?

479
00:36:36,986 --> 00:36:38,780
I thought you were dead.

480
00:36:41,449 --> 00:36:42,575
Dead?

481
00:36:45,120 --> 00:36:46,121
I mean...

482
00:36:47,539 --> 00:36:49,916
I sent you the final payment...

483
00:36:49,999 --> 00:36:51,542
because you said it was taken care of.

484
00:36:51,543 --> 00:36:53,962
But instead of dropping the lawsuit,

485
00:36:54,045 --> 00:36:56,922
that lawyer is now approaching my neighbour...

486
00:36:56,923 --> 00:36:58,466
- to dig up info on me... - Lawyer?

487
00:36:59,300 --> 00:37:00,385
You mean, Choi Sang Cheol?

488
00:37:01,386 --> 00:37:05,890
Yes, I don't know what he's plotting,

489
00:37:05,974 --> 00:37:08,393
but he had a drink with my neighbour...

490
00:37:09,394 --> 00:37:11,228
How on earth did you handle the job...

491
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:13,815
that he's running even wilder now?

492
00:37:14,482 --> 00:37:15,525
Tell me.

493
00:37:27,370 --> 00:37:30,622
Are you trying to play dumb...

494
00:37:30,623 --> 00:37:32,792
after taking all the money?

495
00:37:32,876 --> 00:37:34,961
How can you be...

496
00:37:35,044 --> 00:37:36,337
so rude?

497
00:37:37,005 --> 00:37:39,299
When did you get the message about handling it?

498
00:37:41,259 --> 00:37:42,677
Why would you ask...

499
00:37:46,181 --> 00:37:47,182
Unbelievable.

500
00:37:49,350 --> 00:37:50,351
It was this day.

501
00:37:52,228 --> 00:37:53,521
March 30.

502
00:37:53,980 --> 00:37:57,442
Yes, you messaged me on the 30th.

503
00:37:57,525 --> 00:37:59,652
I wired the money the very next day.

504
00:38:00,487 --> 00:38:02,197
No contact after that?

505
00:38:04,240 --> 00:38:06,910
It's you who didn't answer.

506
00:38:08,953 --> 00:38:11,915
Let's talk about that front door neighbour...

507
00:38:13,082 --> 00:38:15,460
whom you said was with Choi Sang Cheol.

508
00:38:17,212 --> 00:38:18,880
What do you mean, I've changed?

509
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:20,983
I keep bringing up the video, but you never listen.

510
00:38:21,007 --> 00:38:23,551
You stop me from saying anything to your mom.

511
00:38:23,635 --> 00:38:25,552
And earlier, you only took her side.

512
00:38:25,553 --> 00:38:27,514
I didn't take her side.

513
00:38:27,597 --> 00:38:28,932
That's not it.

514
00:38:30,183 --> 00:38:32,685
I told you my parents had a serious fight because of me.

515
00:38:33,353 --> 00:38:35,688
What if they actually get a divorce?

516
00:38:46,407 --> 00:38:47,408
I'm sorry.

517
00:38:48,535 --> 00:38:49,536
It's my fault.

518
00:38:52,121 --> 00:38:53,623
Are you that scared of their divorce?

519
00:38:54,290 --> 00:38:56,376
So much that you can't even ask to delete the video?

520
00:38:57,585 --> 00:39:00,755
No, that's not what I meant.

521
00:39:00,839 --> 00:39:03,591
Then, why are you doing nothing?

522
00:39:03,800 --> 00:39:07,262
How can you be so calm when I'm dying from anxiety?

523
00:39:08,847 --> 00:39:10,139
No, it's just...

524
00:39:10,723 --> 00:39:13,892
my parents have been fighting every day lately.

525
00:39:13,893 --> 00:39:15,478
Is it because you weren't driving?

526
00:39:17,814 --> 00:39:18,898
Hey.

527
00:39:20,900 --> 00:39:22,110
You...

528
00:39:23,361 --> 00:39:25,863
I even lied to my parents to cover for you.

529
00:39:25,864 --> 00:39:27,114
So, you think...

530
00:39:27,115 --> 00:39:29,659
you're innocent and I'm fully in the wrong.

531
00:39:30,785 --> 00:39:34,747
If not, you would've deleted the video yourself a long time ago.

532
00:39:35,582 --> 00:39:36,791
No?

533
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:42,588
She said she'd go home after the meeting?

534
00:39:42,589 --> 00:39:43,964
Okay, bye.

535
00:39:43,965 --> 00:39:45,800
Okay, I'll call you back.

536
00:39:47,927 --> 00:39:48,928
What's wrong?

537
00:39:50,805 --> 00:39:51,806
What is it?

538
00:39:52,599 --> 00:39:53,600
Look.

539
00:39:53,933 --> 00:39:56,811
I'm not sure if I should tell you this because it's only hearsay.

540
00:39:58,479 --> 00:40:00,481
But there's a rumour...

541
00:40:00,565 --> 00:40:03,902
that making Director Kwak the CEO is a condition for the investment.

542
00:40:06,195 --> 00:40:09,741
Along with that, there's talk of embezzlement.

543
00:40:10,950 --> 00:40:14,162
I don't know how much is true,

544
00:40:14,245 --> 00:40:17,332
but you'd better check this quickly.

545
00:40:20,001 --> 00:40:21,377
Excuse me.

546
00:40:24,464 --> 00:40:25,506
Hello?

547
00:40:26,925 --> 00:40:30,762
Publish the investment article on the 13th first,

548
00:40:30,845 --> 00:40:32,430
and then we'll...

549
00:40:32,513 --> 00:40:34,182
One moment.

550
00:40:35,058 --> 00:40:36,184
Why...

551
00:40:38,227 --> 00:40:39,354
What are you...

552
00:40:40,688 --> 00:40:43,191
- Shall I drive you home after this? - Yes.

553
00:40:46,653 --> 00:40:48,112
Hello, ma'am.

554
00:40:48,863 --> 00:40:50,448
How did you know I was here?

555
00:40:50,531 --> 00:40:52,867
I don't like to beat around the bush,

556
00:40:54,410 --> 00:40:55,787
so I'll get straight to the point.

557
00:40:59,832 --> 00:41:01,042
Is the rumour true...

558
00:41:02,418 --> 00:41:05,380
that the condition for the investment is to have Director Kwak...

559
00:41:06,381 --> 00:41:07,382
take my place?

560
00:41:19,060 --> 00:41:21,270
You care so much about reputation...

561
00:41:21,354 --> 00:41:23,606
that you even made our private life an issue.

562
00:41:25,692 --> 00:41:26,693
I'm disappointed in you.

563
00:41:26,776 --> 00:41:28,903
Ms. Park, let's discuss this later.

564
00:41:32,448 --> 00:41:34,575
The brand value of The Zip...

565
00:41:35,243 --> 00:41:36,661
is me, Park Kyung Hee.

566
00:41:37,578 --> 00:41:39,746
If you go ahead with this backroom deal,

567
00:41:39,747 --> 00:41:42,207
my name, my face, and my family are out...

568
00:41:42,208 --> 00:41:43,917
as of that moment.

569
00:41:43,918 --> 00:41:45,586
And it's going to be very loud.

570
00:41:48,715 --> 00:41:51,008
If you want to invest in an empty box of a company...

571
00:41:51,009 --> 00:41:53,761
while tarnishing the reputation you've built up all this time,

572
00:41:54,095 --> 00:41:55,304
please do so.

573
00:42:02,937 --> 00:42:07,066
I really liked this unwavering side of yours.

574
00:42:10,945 --> 00:42:12,280
Have a look.

575
00:42:23,332 --> 00:42:24,459
Well...

576
00:42:25,793 --> 00:42:27,273
This 300 million won was unavoidable.

577
00:42:27,587 --> 00:42:29,963
It happened while paying for materials upfront...

578
00:42:29,964 --> 00:42:33,301
Wouldn't it be better to remain as the face of The Zip...

579
00:42:34,218 --> 00:42:38,639
rather than a criminal who embezzled her company's money?

580
00:42:45,980 --> 00:42:47,023
Kyung Hee.

581
00:42:47,523 --> 00:42:51,360
Think about what's best for the company.

582
00:42:51,444 --> 00:42:52,445
Okay?

583
00:43:02,872 --> 00:43:03,873
Hey.

584
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:07,085
What?

585
00:43:09,670 --> 00:43:11,590
Did you rat me out to Michelle for embezzling...

586
00:43:12,256 --> 00:43:14,675
so you could take over the company?

587
00:44:03,599 --> 00:44:04,934
Are you okay?

588
00:44:05,017 --> 00:44:06,894
Oh, I'm all right.

589
00:44:08,354 --> 00:44:09,772
Well, I got...

590
00:44:10,898 --> 00:44:12,316
so worried about you.

591
00:44:14,402 --> 00:44:15,944
It's okay.

592
00:44:15,945 --> 00:44:17,446
Are you sure...

593
00:44:17,530 --> 00:44:19,657
you can drive?

594
00:44:20,032 --> 00:44:21,576
I'm good.

595
00:44:22,660 --> 00:44:24,036
I'm really okay.

596
00:44:26,539 --> 00:44:29,208
This is hardly a rare occurrence in business.

597
00:44:30,084 --> 00:44:32,003
Anyway, I'm sorry about today.

598
00:44:32,795 --> 00:44:34,045
We didn't get to talk business.

599
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:35,173
- It's my fault. - Come on.

600
00:44:35,840 --> 00:44:37,592
Please don't say that.

601
00:44:42,054 --> 00:44:43,055
Kyung Hee.

602
00:44:45,141 --> 00:44:46,267
When things are tough,

603
00:44:48,436 --> 00:44:49,437
it's okay...

604
00:44:50,021 --> 00:44:51,480
to admit it.

605
00:44:52,940 --> 00:44:53,941
It's fine.

606
00:45:00,531 --> 00:45:01,699
It's all right.

607
00:45:03,868 --> 00:45:04,869
It's okay.

608
00:45:09,832 --> 00:45:10,833
It's okay.

609
00:45:14,754 --> 00:45:15,922
It's okay.

610
00:45:18,466 --> 00:45:19,508
That's okay.

611
00:45:20,801 --> 00:45:22,385
It's all right.

612
00:45:22,386 --> 00:45:25,431
- Oh, my. I... - Yes?

613
00:45:25,681 --> 00:45:26,766
- Oh, gosh. - Excuse me.

614
00:45:30,144 --> 00:45:32,230
I'm sorry if I overstepped.

615
00:45:37,693 --> 00:45:39,654
I'll get going now.

616
00:45:40,947 --> 00:45:42,698
Please be careful on the road.

617
00:45:44,784 --> 00:45:45,785
All right.

618
00:45:53,709 --> 00:45:55,127
Take care.

619
00:46:14,063 --> 00:46:17,108
(Gogo Used Goods: How did Sang Cheol find out about us?)

620
00:46:19,568 --> 00:46:20,987
(I don't know.)

621
00:46:24,949 --> 00:46:26,284
(Was he following us?)

622
00:46:26,367 --> 00:46:29,167
(If he knew it all, why would he approach me? What else does he want?)

623
00:46:33,040 --> 00:46:34,542
(It can't be...)

624
00:46:34,625 --> 00:46:35,960
(our video, can it?)

625
00:46:37,920 --> 00:46:38,963
The video?

626
00:46:49,432 --> 00:46:52,267
(Can you use that detective agency I recommended to dig into him?)

627
00:46:52,268 --> 00:46:53,894
(If this gets out, I'll be finished.)

628
00:46:55,563 --> 00:46:57,064
He's got to be kidding me.

629
00:46:59,317 --> 00:47:02,236
(That agency you introduced is exactly why I'm...)

630
00:47:05,114 --> 00:47:06,281
(That guy has been ignoring my calls...)

631
00:47:06,282 --> 00:47:07,657
(and acting weird since he met Choi Sang Cheol.)

632
00:47:07,658 --> 00:47:09,538
(I went to see him, but he hardly even talked.)

633
00:47:10,786 --> 00:47:12,455
(What if they're in on it together?)

634
00:47:15,291 --> 00:47:17,460
Choi Sang Cheol and Na Sol?

635
00:47:22,006 --> 00:47:24,884
(Did a man named Na Sol come see you?)

636
00:47:25,634 --> 00:47:27,011
Spin and kick!

637
00:47:27,553 --> 00:47:30,014
- See? It's awesome. - Sorry?

638
00:47:30,556 --> 00:47:32,475
Yes, it's incredible.

639
00:47:38,647 --> 00:47:40,566
(What does the agency guy look like?)

640
00:47:46,655 --> 00:47:49,617
Dodge, swing, then a backspin!

641
00:47:57,124 --> 00:47:58,125
What is it?

642
00:47:58,667 --> 00:47:59,794
Is everything all right?

643
00:47:59,835 --> 00:48:01,003
What? Oh, sorry.

644
00:48:01,087 --> 00:48:03,589
My phone fell out of my pocket.

645
00:48:04,673 --> 00:48:06,425
Are you okay with this?

646
00:48:06,509 --> 00:48:08,260
- The backspin. - Yes, no problem.

647
00:48:08,344 --> 00:48:09,345
It's cool.

648
00:48:09,720 --> 00:48:10,720
- Can you do it? - Yes.

649
00:48:10,721 --> 00:48:11,846
You can handle it, right?

650
00:48:11,847 --> 00:48:13,307
Yes, it shouldn't be a problem.

651
00:48:14,141 --> 00:48:15,976
Okay, perfect.

652
00:48:16,060 --> 00:48:17,978
Let's keep this momentum.

653
00:48:18,062 --> 00:48:20,398
- Got it. - Sang Yong, move it!

654
00:49:04,775 --> 00:49:07,736
(Ye Ji)

655
00:49:11,907 --> 00:49:15,035
(Mom, did you make sure Ye Ji's mom deleted the video?)

656
00:49:29,842 --> 00:49:32,802
Are you okay? Want me to take you to the hospital?

657
00:49:32,803 --> 00:49:34,637
Forget it. I'm tired. Let's just go home.

658
00:49:34,638 --> 00:49:35,639
- Hurry. - Okay.

659
00:50:06,212 --> 00:50:07,213
Wait.

660
00:50:08,797 --> 00:50:09,798
What was that?

661
00:51:03,310 --> 00:51:04,311
(Condoms)

662
00:51:29,587 --> 00:51:31,130
Take care.

663
00:51:40,681 --> 00:51:42,349
Where is it?

664
00:51:46,854 --> 00:51:48,063
There it is.

665
00:51:57,114 --> 00:51:58,115
Dr. Joo?

666
00:52:01,076 --> 00:52:02,328
What are you still doing here?

667
00:52:03,329 --> 00:52:05,331
I'm looking for the exit.

668
00:52:06,040 --> 00:52:08,584
I don't have my car now.

669
00:52:13,797 --> 00:52:15,174
Get in.

670
00:52:28,145 --> 00:52:29,146
Just a little, yes.

671
00:52:29,938 --> 00:52:31,565
What's wrong with me?

672
00:52:31,649 --> 00:52:32,733
One second.

673
00:52:32,816 --> 00:52:34,360
It'll be ready soon.

674
00:52:34,943 --> 00:52:36,445
I don't get it.

675
00:52:36,654 --> 00:52:38,489
This never happens to me.

676
00:52:38,572 --> 00:52:39,573
- Dr. Joo. - One second.

677
00:52:39,657 --> 00:52:41,033
- Dr. Joo. - I'm not like this.

678
00:52:41,116 --> 00:52:42,409
I don't think this is right.

679
00:52:42,951 --> 00:52:43,994
What...

680
00:52:44,078 --> 00:52:46,080
- Kyung Hee, it's working. - Oh, my.

681
00:52:46,163 --> 00:52:47,247
It's almost there.

682
00:52:48,332 --> 00:52:49,333
Oh, my gosh.

683
00:52:58,342 --> 00:52:59,343
Min Seo?
